linux-revpi-v8 (6.6.46-rt39-revpi7-1+deb12+1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * The revpi-eeprom overlay now automatically selects the correct
    configuration based on your device's SoC, eliminating the need for manual
    setup.
  * Because the PiBridge cannot guarantee packets reach their destination,
    errors happen occasionally. This is okay because the protocol deals with
    these errors without restricting functionality and reliability. Instead of
    printing every single error in the kernel log, they are only printed when a
    threshold is reached that indicates a connection problem. To ensure error
    information is not lost, these errors are now published in the sysfs under
    /sys/bus/serial/drivers/pi-bridge/stats/ for inspection.
  * Unused HDMI ports on Connect 4, Connect 5, and Flat S devices are now
    disabled, ensuring only active audio and video interfaces are displayed in
    the system.
  * Fixed CAN termination settings to ensure compatibility with systems using
    GPIOs behind I2C expanders, improving overall reliability.
  * Integrated the I2C controller directly into the system to prevent rare
    startup issues related to display initialization.
  * Enabled support for updating the bootloader EEPROM directly on
    Connect 4/Flat-S devices without additional hardware steps.

 -- Ramiro Gsponer <r.gsponer@kunbus.com>  Wed, 12 Feb 2025 17:20:11 +0000

linux-revpi-v8 (6.6.46-rt39-revpi6-1+deb12+1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Fixed a bug where the LAN B (eth1) interface could become unresponsive.
  This issue was caused by the ASPM power management functions for the
  PCIe controller. To address this, ASPM has been disabled for the PCIe
  controller.

 -- Philipp Rosenberger <p.rosenberger@kunbus.com>  Wed, 27 Nov 2024 15:24:25 +0100
